        "st8": {"v": 1, "quote": "Bart Ehrman introduces this question in The Evidence for Jesus, his volume. And he takes 20 pages by telling you why the mythicists don't line up."}
      },
      "prior_art": "Bart Ehrman, The Evidence for Jesus (mythicism critique), 2024",
      "originality": {
        "or1": {"v": 1, "quote": "Bart Ehrman introduces this question in The Evidence for Jesus, his volume. And he takes 20 pages by telling you why the mythicists don't line up.", "why": "It largely restates Ehrman's critique but adapts it to Habermas's own inclusion criteria."},
        "or2": {"v": 1, "quote": "He claims to have a PhD and be an expert in ancient um ancient subjects and languages, and has no college degrees.", "why": "It adds the specific credential-fraud anecdote as new evidence."},
        "or3": {"v": 0, "quote": ""},
        "or4": {"v": 0, "quote": ""}
      },
      "weakest_link": "P2: Ehrman's 'nobody likes them' is an appeal to popularity rather than evidence that mythicists are wrong.",
      "develop_next": "Give the actual credential criteria and apply them to named mythicists, rather than resting on Ehrman's authority and an anecdote.",
